Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='triagecards', at=datetime(2026, 10, 24, 0, 0, 0), actor='owner', title="The triage agent's writes do not reach a chain; they are cards in the Inbox the owner taps", body="⚠️ *The agent's writes do not reach a chain; they are cards* (2026-10-24, ARCHITECTURE §10.6; the owner: one path for every change that waits for his tap). The triage agent's `todo_add`, `todo_update` and `record` are the SAME verb types the secretary holds (`agent::verbs::{TodoAdd, TodoUpdate, Record}`, generic over `agent::Holds`): each builds one `changes::Act` and hands it to its surface's `Holds::write`. The secretary's performs it at once as `assistant`; the agent's files it through `secretary::filed::TriageCards`, the one door the agent's call holds (its stores are private and its one method files as `Proposer::Triage`, stored `Triaged`), as a `Proposal::Changes` card in the Inbox, joining the open triage card about the same todo so the Inbox holds one card per todo, after building it against the chain as the tap will. Only the owner's tap performs a card (the one performer, `changes::apply`, as `assistant`); its `why` and `sources` are the agent's, required, and the card says who asked. The agent's `chain` is still a REPLICA of its target (`events-triage/`), synced before a run and READ; nothing appends to it. The fence is unchanged (same `tool-guard.sh`, `agent::VERBS`, `WRITES_AS`, snapshot). The open batches written before this are carried into cards by `suzatary proposals carry` (dry run first, `--apply` after the deploy with the owner's yes); that verb, `secretary::batch_cards` and the replica's files go in its follow-up.", rationale='The owner, 2026-10-24 (ARCHITECTURE §10.6): one path for every change that waits for his tap.', supersedes=()))